  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<div class=\"desc\"><p>The move constructor is treated in a way that allows returning an instance from a function. Typically, the move constructor is only declared, but not defined. This allows a C++14-compliant compiler to use RVO (Return Value Optimization) to return an instance from a factory-like function.</p></div>",
